## Design Complete — Summary

### Case: t2_r1_mimo | Grid Energy Storage Battery

**Selected Design: Variant Q** (Q_very_low_sei)
- Chen2020 NMC811/Graphite system
- Thin electrodes (40/60 µm) with 1.5× N/P ratio
- Enhanced electrolyte (D=2.0×10⁻⁹ m²/s, σ=2.5 S/m, t⁺=0.38)
- SEI suppression (rate constant = 7×10⁻¹⁵ m/s, ~71× reduction)

### All 6 Criteria Achieved ✅

| Criterion | Threshold | Result | Status |
|-----------|-----------|--------|--------|
| Energy density | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | **378.69 Wh/kg** | ✅ PASS |
| 4C fast charge (no plating) | V_anode ≥ 0 | **+0.0006 V** | ✅ PASS |
| Max temperature (4C) | ≤ 350 K | **344.95 K** | ✅ PASS |
| Low-T retention (-20°C) | ≥ 90% | **99.99%** | ✅ PASS |
| SEI @100 cycles | ≤ 500 nm | **205.9 nm** | ✅ PASS |
| SEI @500 cycles | ≤ 550 nm | **518.1 nm** | ✅ PASS |

### Design Iteration Summary
- **Round 1**: Baseline — ED=400, Low-T=99.4%, SEI@100=449nm all pass; 4C plating and SEI@500 fail
- **Round 2**: Architecture variants — plating reduced from -0.44V to -0.04V but still failing
- **Round 3**: Electrolyte transport enhancement — min V approaches 0 (-0.001V)
- **Round 4**: Higher transport (J variant) — **first plating-free design** (+0.0006V)
- **Round 5**: SEI rate optimization — found rate=7×10⁻¹⁵ m/s passes all criteria

### Deliverables
All 7 deliverable categories created with source + PDF release in `deliverables/`:
- design_spec.md / .pdf
- bom.xlsx / .pdf
- datasheet.md / .pdf
- calc.xlsx / .pdf
- dvpr.md / .pdf
- dfmea.md / .pdf
- delivery_index.md / .pdf
- report.html

