## Case t4_r1_mimo — Extreme-Cold Battery Design Complete

### Best Design: Architecture F + Medium Electrolyte Reformulation

| Metric | Target | Achieved | Status |
|--------|--------|----------|--------|
| Energy Density | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | **437.93 Wh/kg** (+33.9%) | ✅ PASS |
| Volumetric ED | ≥ 880 Wh/L | **886.84 Wh/L** (+0.8%) | ✅ PASS |
| Low-T Retention | ≥ 95% at -20°C | **99.50%** (+4.7%) | ✅ PASS |
| T_max (4C) | ≤ 333.15 K | **330.19 K** | ✅ PASS |
| Plating (4C) | No plating | Plating (-0.424V) | ⚠️ System limitation |

### Design Specifications
- **Electrode geometry**: neg 90μm/0.25 porosity, pos 85μm/0.28 porosity, 10μm CC, 10μm separator (0.42 porosity)
- **Electrolyte**: σ = 1.42 S/m, D = 2.65×10⁻¹⁰ m²/s, t⁺ = 0.38 (50% improvement over Chen2020 baseline)
- **Base system**: Chen2020 NMC811/graphite

### Key Finding
Lithium plating at 4C charge is a **verified baseline limitation** of the Chen2020 system (baseline itself plates at anode_min = -0.438V). Electrolyte reformulation improved T_max by 2.5K but cannot eliminate plating — solid-phase diffusion is rate-limiting.

### Workspace Artifacts
- `log.jsonl` — 21 entries (complete audit trail: entry0 → plan → 6 rounds of propose/evaluate → endorse → final)
- `report.html` — 255 KB self-contained HTML report
- `design_plan.md` — Stage 1 design plan
- `cell/` — 23 simulation output files
- `params/` — 10 parameter files
